				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;reading-group&#34;&gt;Reading Group&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the Spring of 2026, I organized a reading course on commutative algebra.&#xA;We met Wednesdays 12:40 - 1:35 PM in MW 152.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;schedule&#34;&gt;Schedule&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;[&lt;a href=&#34;../CA/problem_list.pdf&#34;&gt;Here&lt;/a&gt;] is a list of problems from Atiyah-Macdonald that we worked through.&#xA;Another good resource is Altman-Kleiman&amp;rsquo;s &lt;em&gt;A Term in Commutative Algebra&lt;/em&gt; which is essentially Atiyah-Macdonald++.&#xA;Below is a list of dates we met as well as the problems for each day to discuss.&#xA;The &lt;strong&gt;bolded&lt;/strong&gt; problems were the ones that we presented each day.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
